#type	charge(e)	radius(A)	epsilon(kJ.mol-1) 	mass(Da)	transferIMP(kJ.mol-1.A-2)	Hydrophobicity(sqrt(kJ.mol-1.A-1))
# NOTE: this file used to carry an EIGHTH, unnamed column of 0.0 on every
# line while its own header declared seven names. ForceFieldReader accepts
# six or seven columns and calls die() otherwise, so the file could not be
# loaded at all. The unnamed column is gone.
#
# Its Hydrophobicity is 1.00 for all twenty residues, which is a flag ("treat
# every residue as hydrophobic") and not a scale: the pairwise law is a
# product, so every pair gets the same amplitude and the term cannot tell
# leucine from lysine. Use it to switch the term on, not to model anything.
ACA	0.00	5.2	0.87864	89.00	3.0	1.00
